2. Integration Architecture and File Responsibilities
This section explains the actual project structure behind the Jira integration.



JiraFlowCoordinator → Orchestrates the workflow.
JiraTestPlanManager → Resolves or creates Test Plans.
JiraExecutionPublisher → Publishes executions and attachments.
JiraGateway → Calls the endpoints.
JiraGaiaReportBuilder → Prepares report data.
JiraGaiaHtmlTemplateBuilder → Renders the final HTML.


JiraFlowCoordinator is the main orchestration class of the integration. It is responsible for centralizing the base configuration, resolving the correct report folder, identifying the suite name, generating the execution and Test Plan names, finding the XML result file, collecting failure image candidates, and triggering the full Jira publishing flow in the correct order by calling the report builder, Test Plan manager, and execution publisher. This is the right file to update when you need to change global Jira settings, naming rules, XML priority, report folder resolution, or the overall execution sequence.
🔗 Full page:  eMatch JiraFlowCoordinator



JiraGateway is the Jira communication layer and contains the logic that actually sends requests to Jira and interprets the responses. It validates the required configuration, imports XML execution results, searches for existing Test Plans, retrieves issues by key, creates new Test Plans, links Test Executions to Test Plans, updates execution metadata, and uploads attachments. This is the file to change when you need to adjust request behavior, authentication, response parsing, accepted status codes, or add new Jira API actions.
🔗 Full page:  eMatch JiraGateway



JiraTestPlanManager is responsible for deciding whether the current execution should reuse an existing Test Plan or create a new one. It checks force-create rules, manual overrides, previously saved Test Plan keys, validates whether a saved key still matches the current suite, searches Jira for an exact matching Test Plan, selects the newest valid result, and saves the resolved key locally for future reuse. This is the correct file to update when you want to change the reuse strategy, matching rules, saved key validation, or the conditions for creating a new Test Plan.
🔗 Full page: eMatch JiraTestPlanManager



JiraExecutionPublisher handles the publishing stage after the Test Plan has already been resolved. It imports execution results into Jira, adds the created execution to the Test Plan, updates the execution summary, labels, and environment, locates the generated GAIA report, creates Results.zip and Evidences.zip, uploads all attachments, and skips locked, unreadable, or excluded files during packaging. This is the file to update when you need to change ZIP content rules, attachment upload order, excluded folders or files, or the publishing sequence after execution creation.
🔗 Full page: eMatch JiraExecutionPublisher



JiraGaiaReportBuilder is responsible for generating the custom gaiaReport.html file that is later attached to the Jira Test Execution. It parses XML execution results and execution logs, builds and enriches scenario data, creates fallback scenarios when log information is missing, normalizes scenario steps, applies timing fallback logic, finds and attaches failed evidence images, and prepares the final model used by the HTML template before writing the report file into the report folder. This is the file to change when you need to adjust log parsing, scenario extraction, fallback behavior, timing calculation, screenshot matching, error summary logic, or the report generation flow before rendering.
🔗 Full page: eMatch JiraReportBuilder



JiraGaiaHtmlTemplateBuilder is the visual rendering layer of the GAIA custom report and is responsible for transforming the normalized execution model into the final interactive HTML page attached to Jira. It builds the full report structure, including header, scenario list, scenario detail panels, steps table, failed evidence block, charts, CSS styling, and JavaScript interactions such as tabs and filtering. This is the right file to change when you need to update the report layout, labels, colors, status presentation, charts, evidence display, sidebar behavior, or any other visual and front-end aspect of gaiaReport.html. 🔗 Full page: [Add link here]
